# Function complexity

A new or rewritten function stays at cyclomatic complexity 20 or under. That is 1, plus one for each `if`, loop, `case`, `catch`, ternary, and `&&`, `||`, or `??`. Nested functions are counted on their own.

Do not split an existing function only to lower its score. Threshold tables such as `cat`, `problemOf`, and `planNeeds` stay in one function: the score is the medical rules.

When a function you are already editing mixes two jobs, split the jobs. A sign-in screen template and the decision of which queue error to show are separate functions. A list of blood-pressure cutoffs is one function.

```javascript
// Two jobs in one function. Split them.
async function queueSync(manual) {
  const rows = await loadQueuePages(manual);
  applyQueueRows(rows);
}

function queueSyncError(err) {
  if (isMissingTable(err)) return 'The live queue is not set up yet.';
  if (!navigator.onLine) return 'Could not reach the server yet — retrying.';
  return 'The queue could not load.';
}
```
